# SP11 step 1: compose/status/index.ts is the public, read-only view.
# Format: file | regular expression the file must contain | message if it doesn't
compose/status/index.ts | req\.method !== "GET" | must serve GET only and answer 405 to anything else
compose/status/index.ts | res\.writeHead\(405\) | must answer 405 to a method it does not serve
compose/status/index.ts | SELECT count\(\*\)::int AS n FROM events | must report how many events were processed
compose/status/index.ts | xLen\("events-dead"\) | must report the dead-letter depth
compose/status/index.ts | content-type": *"application/json | must answer JSON
compose/status/index.ts | processed: rows\[0\]\.n, deadLetterDepth: dead | must answer the two numbers the README promises
compose/status/package.json | "redis": "\^5\.0\.0" | the status service must use redis 5, the major the reference build runs
compose/status/Dockerfile | ^RUN npm install$ | the build must install dependencies without a lock, because these folders commit none
compose/status/Dockerfile | !^RUN npm ci$ | npm ci needs a lock file, and this folder has none
